<title>UK: ABF yr pretax rises to 430 million stg.</title>
<headline>ABF yr pretax rises to 430 million stg.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to September 14</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		31.0		   vs 27.8</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 5.25		   vs 4.5</p>
<p> Pretax		     430		    vs 375</p>
<p> Turnover		   5,707		  vs 4,894</p>
<p> Operating result	 395		    vs 335</p>
<p> Exceptional income     6.0		    vs nil</p>
<p> Investment income	54		     vs 69</p>
<p> Interest		   25		     vs 29</p>
<p> Tax			  114		    vs 119</p>
<p> Net taxed		  286		    vs 256</p>
<p> Attributable	     278		    vs 250</p>
<p> Pay date		   March 3, 1997</p>
<p> Div registration date  February 4, 1997  Ex-div date		January 27, 1997</p>
<p>NOTE - ABF said its total retail results included a benefit arising from a changed currency translation rate on sales and profits of 29 million stg and 2.0 million stg respectively.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
